<title>USA: TABLE - Keystone International Q2 shr up.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Keystone International Q2 shr up.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>For the quarter ended</p>
<p>		     June 27, 1997(a)	  June 30, 1996</p>
<p> Shr		 $	 0.38	   $	 0.30</p>
<p> Net			 13,500		   10,700</p>
<p> Revs		     173,200		  173,600</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  35,600		   35,500</p>
<p>6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $	 0.65	   $	 0.56</p>
<p> Net			 23,000		   20,000</p>
<p> Revs		     331,200		  337,800</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  35,600		   35,500</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>(a) Effective in fiscal 1997, the company changed its fiscal year to consist of three 13-week periods plus the fourth period which ends on December 31.</p>
<p>The company said that without the impact of the stronger dollar, second quarter sales would have been 3.0 percent higher than 1996 level.</p>
<p>Full company name is Keystone International Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 201 859-1610))</p>
